%S A123453 1,2,4,11,33,145,826,6266,54401,504200,4801753,46861427,474467542
%N A123453 Number of skeletal perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123453 A graph is skeletal if it can be obtained from a parity graph by removing the edges of a collection of stars (subgraphs K_{1,t}, t >= 1), such that no two star centers are joined by an induced path of length at most 2. These graphs are perfect, and the class is closed under induced subgraphs. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 07 2026
%H A123453 S. Hougardy, <a href="http://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
%H A123453 S. Hougardy, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.disc.2006.05.021">Classes of perfect graphs</a>, Discr. Math. 306 (2006), 2529-2571.
%Y A123453 Cf. A000088, A052431 (perfect graphs), A123443 (parity graphs).
